meta {
  name: Update Radiology Test
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/master-data/{{masterDataId}}/radiology-tests/{{radiologyTestId}}
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

vars:pre-request {
  masterDataId: 2db13b5e-4a25-412f-bcd9-68bcbeea9d59
}

body:json {
  {
    "testDisplayName": "CT Chest (revised)",
    "isContrast": true,
    "priceMsrp": 4800,
    "priceMaximum": 4500,
    "priceMinimum": 3200,
    "isActive": true,
    "remarks": "Updated protocol note"
  }
}

docs {
  🔒 **RBAC:** requires `business_admin:master_data__update_test` — enforced by
  `PermissionGuard`; admins bypass, so `{{businessAccessToken}}` succeeds.

  Update a radiology test's scalar fields. Every field is **optional** — omitted
  fields are left unchanged (partial update). Scope (`tenantId`/`branchId`/
  `masterDataId`) is never in the body. The full editable field set mirrors Create
  Radiology Test (identity, radiology classification, logical refs, pricing, TAT,
  schedule, flags, status, notes).

  Price ordering (`priceMinimum ≤ priceMaximum ≤ priceMsrp`) is validated against
  the **merged** values → 422 `VALIDATION_ERROR` on violation. `testName` /
  `testCode` stay unique per master data among active rows → 409
  `RADIOLOGY_TEST_NAME_CONFLICT` / `RADIOLOGY_TEST_CODE_CONFLICT`. 404
  `RADIOLOGY_TEST_NOT_FOUND` if the id isn't a live test here.

  > `code` and any list price are system-set — never send them.
}
